.TH KILN 1 "2026-03-16" "kiln" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
kiln \- a build system with Tcl-based build descriptions
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kiln
.RI [ options ]
.RI [ target .\|.\|.]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kiln
is a build system that reads build descriptions written in Tcl
(called Kilnfiles) and executes commands in dependency order.
It uses a DAG of file and command nodes, hybrid staleness detection
(stat fingerprint + content hash + command string hash), and
compiler depfile parsing for automatic header dependencies.
.PP
Build artifacts are placed in
.IR build/<triplet>/ ,
where
.I <triplet>
is the target toolchain identifier (e.g.\&
.IR x86_64-linux-gnu ).
The triplet is detected automatically via
.B cc \-dumpmachine
or set explicitly with
.BR \-\-triplet .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-a " action" "\fR,\fP \-\-action " action
Run a built-in action instead of building targets.
See
.B ACTIONS
below.
.TP
.BI \-\-triplet " triplet"
Set the target triplet explicitly, skipping
.B cc \-dumpmachine
detection.
.TP
.BI \-\-lib " file.tcl"
Load a Tcl library file before evaluating Kilnfiles.
May be specified multiple times; files are loaded in order.
Libraries define procs that Kilnfiles can call.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-stdlib
Skip loading the built-in standard library
.RI ( kiln.tcl ).
Combine with
.B \-\-lib
to substitute a custom standard library.
.TP
.BR \-n ", " \-\-dry\-run
Print commands that would be executed without running them.
.TP
.BI \-j " N"
Run up to
.I N
jobs in parallel.
Defaults to the number of online CPUs.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print a usage summary and exit.
.SH ACTIONS
Actions are invoked with
.B \-a
and perform operations other than building targets.
Using a flag rather than positional arguments avoids ambiguity
when a build target shares a name with an action.
.TP
.B clean
Delete all output files declared in the DAG and remove any
parent directories that become empty.
Also removes the staleness database
.RI ( kiln.cdb )
and the build directory if empty.
.TP
.B status
Report inconsistencies between the staleness database and the
current DAG.
.I (Not yet implemented.)
.SH KILNFILE SYNTAX
Build descriptions are Tcl scripts.
kiln extends the Tcl interpreter with the following commands:
.SS Build Commands
.TP
.BI "rule " "outputs " { " body " }
Define a build rule.
.I outputs
is a Tcl list of output file paths.
The
.I body
is evaluated in Tcl context and may call:
.RS
.TP
.BI "inputs " files...
Declare input files.
Sets the variable
.BR $in .
May be called multiple times; inputs accumulate.
.TP
.BI "command " {template}
Set the shell command to execute.
The template is evaluated after the body completes,
so
.BR $out ", " $in ", and " $depfile
are all available for substitution.
Enclose in braces to defer expansion.
.TP
.BI "depfile " path
Declare a compiler-generated dependency file
(e.g.\& from
.BR "cc \-MMD" ).
Sets the variable
.BR $depfile .
.RE
.TP
.BI "source " filename
Read and evaluate another Tcl file.
Searches the current directory first, then each directory in the
.B $SourcePath
variable.
.SS Tcl Extensions
.TP
.BI "glob " "pattern ..."
Return a space-separated list of files matching the given
shell glob patterns.
Elements containing whitespace are brace-quoted.
.TP
.BI "file " "subcommand arg"
Path manipulation.
Subcommands:
.BR dirname ,
.BR tail ,
.BR extension ,
.BR rootname .
.TP
.BI "lindex " "list index"
Return element
.I index
from a Tcl list.
.TP
.BI "llength " list
Return the number of elements in a Tcl list.
.SS Predefined Variables
.TP
.B $Triplet
The target triplet string.
.TP
.B $Jobs
Number of parallel jobs.
.TP
.B $DryRun
.B 1
if
.B \-\-dry\-run
was specified, otherwise
.BR 0 .
.TP
.B $SourcePath
Space-separated list of directories searched by
.BR source .
.SH STALENESS DETECTION
kiln uses a two-level check for each input file:
.IP 1. 4
Compare the stat fingerprint (mtime, size, inode, ctime) against
the value stored in
.IR kiln.cdb .
If it matches, the file is unchanged (fast path).
.IP 2. 4
If the stat differs, hash the file contents and compare against the
stored hash.
If the hash matches, the file was touched but not modified
(e.g.\&
.BR touch ).
.PP
The command string for each rule is also hashed.
Changing compiler flags or other command arguments triggers a rebuild
even if no input files changed.
.PP
Compiler-generated depfiles
.RB ( "cc \-MMD" )
are parsed after each compilation to discover implicit header
dependencies.
These are stored in
.I kiln.cdb
and checked for staleness on subsequent builds.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I Kilnfile
Build description file (Tcl script).
.TP
.IR build/<triplet>/
Directory for build artifacts.
.TP
.IR build/<triplet>/kiln.cdb
Persistent staleness database (CDB format).
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
All targets are up to date or were built successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A build command failed, a cycle was detected, or an error occurred.
.SH EXAMPLES
Build a project:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kiln Kilnfile
.fi
.RE
.PP
Clean all outputs:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kiln -a clean Kilnfile
.fi
.RE
.PP
Dry run with explicit triplet:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kiln -n --triplet arm-linux-gnueabihf Kilnfile
.fi
.RE
.PP
Use a custom library instead of the standard library:
.PP
.RS
.nf
kiln --no-stdlib --lib my-stdlib.tcl Kilnfile
.fi
.RE
.PP
Example Kilnfile:
.PP
.RS
.nf
set cflags "-Wall -O2"

rule build/$Triplet/hello.o {
    inputs hello.c
    depfile build/$Triplet/hello.d
    command {cc $cflags -c -o $out $in -MMD -MF $depfile}
}

rule build/$Triplet/hello {
    inputs build/$Triplet/hello.o
    command {cc -o $out $in}
}
.fi
.RE
